Bundled in the desktop app
==========================

CPython, 78 Python packages (among them Microsoft MarkItDown, FastAPI,
pywebview and pypdfium2/PDFium), and the JavaScript libraries marked,
DOMPurify and highlight.js, each under its own license. The Python packages
include SpeechRecognition, which ships FLAC encoder
binaries licensed under GPL-2.0. Texts: LICENSES/python-packages-desktop.txt
and the other files in LICENSES/.

Optional components (downloaded only when you choose to)
=========================================================

Docling engine pack
  Built by InkDoc from the upstream projects and hosted on InkDoc's own GitHub
  release (docling-pack-v1), not downloaded from the Docling project.
  Contains Docling (MIT, https://github.com/docling-project/docling), the
  "heron" layout model weights (Apache-2.0), the TableFormer weights
  (CDLA-Permissive-2.0), RapidOCR and its PP-OCR models (Apache-2.0), a CPython
  runtime, and 107 Python packages under their own licenses, some of
  which bundle LGPL libraries. See LICENSES/docling-pack-packages.md.

Code & Formula Recognition add-on
  docling-project/CodeFormulaV2 model weights (CDLA-Permissive-2.0), hosted on
  InkDoc's GitHub release docling-addon-v1.

GLM-OCR model (GGUF build) and llama.cpp
  Model:    zai-org/GLM-OCR          https://huggingface.co/zai-org/GLM-OCR
  GGUF:     ggml-org/GLM-OCR-GGUF    https://huggingface.co/ggml-org/GLM-OCR-GGUF
  License:  MIT (per the model card)
  Runtime:  ggml-org/llama.cpp       https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp
  License:  MIT, Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors; the Windows builds
            also contain the LLVM OpenMP runtime (Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception)
  Downloaded from the official source first, and from InkDoc's GitHub mirror
  (byte-identical copies) as a fallback, verified against SHA-256 hashes
  pinned in InkDoc. The GLM-OCR and llama.cpp license texts are installed next
  to them (<engines folder>/glm-ocr/licenses/) and ship inside InkDoc in
  app/core/assets/licenses/. InkDoc uses the model only. It does not use the
  GLM-OCR SDK or the PP-DocLayoutV3 layout model (both Apache License 2.0).
